The application must not execute every workload on one thread.

Use a managed architecture.

11.1 Thread Responsibilities

Android Main Thread

- Android lifecycle.
- Lightweight UI interactions.
- Navigation.
- Settings.
- Input dispatch.

Render Thread

- OpenGL rendering.
- Camera.
- Mesh rendering.
- Shader operations.
- GPU resource management.

Physics Worker

- Rigid body simulation.
- Collision processing.
- Physics constraints.
- Object state updates.

Animation Worker

- Animation evaluation.
- Skeletal transforms.
- IK.
- Pose blending.

Asset Workers

- GLB loading.
- Texture decoding.
- Mesh processing.
- Material preparation.
- Asset validation.

Background Save Worker

- Scene serialization.
- Save files.
- Autosave.
- Loading.

11.2 Thread Safety

Use:

- Kotlin Coroutines.
- ExecutorService.
- Thread-safe queues.
- Immutable snapshots.
- Double buffering.
- Atomic state exchange.

Avoid:

- Race conditions.
- Deadlocks.
- Excessive locks.
- Uncontrolled thread creation.
- Main-thread blocking.

OpenGL context operations must remain on the valid context-owning render thread.

